From 444dbd4d5d63cf673b8787124d12ac4e19cb65e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:14:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 44/82] sunxi: h713: let the board say which project it is, not
 the command line

"h713_disp init" required the project ID as an argument, and the boot
script supplies it from h713_project. That is right for our layout -- the
installer writes the variable from the device's own panel_config.ini --
but it is the only way in, so a device without our environment has no
answer at all: the probe, a FEL run, a saved environment from before the
variable existed, or the bootcmd itself, where "h713_disp init
${h713_project}" with the variable unset expands to a bare "h713_disp
init" and printed usage.

Make the ID optional and, when it is missing, ask the board. First
h713_project, which is the installed case. Then panel_config.ini, which
is where the vendor keeps it: on Reserve0, mirrored to media_data (/oem),
found by name and slot, and stating the ID in decimal -- "ProjectID = 52"
is 0x34 -- where the TSE file names and this code are hexadecimal. A
stock device answers from that alone, which is what the probe needs.

The ID is now simply the first argument that is not a flag, so every
existing invocation keeps its meaning and the flags may precede it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
